.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt NOTIFY_WATCH 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm notify_watch_create ,
.Nm notify_watch_destroy ,
.Nm notify_watch_publish ,
.Nm notify_watch_open ,
.Nm notify_watch_close ,
.Nm notify_watch_begin ,
.Nm notify_watch_cancel ,
.Nm notify_watch_take
.Nd bounded provider-side snapshot and watch storage
.Sh LIBRARY
Notification Library (libnotify, \-lnotify)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In notify_watch.h
.Ft int
.Fn notify_watch_create "size_t capacity" "size_t subscribers" "struct notify_watch **result"
.Ft int
.Fn notify_watch_destroy "struct notify_watch *store"
.Ft int
.Fn notify_watch_publish "struct notify_watch *store" "const void *data" "size_t length"
.Ft int
.Fn notify_watch_open "struct notify_watch *store" "const struct notify_watch_cursor *resume" "struct notify_watcher **result"
.Ft void
.Fn notify_watch_close "struct notify_watcher *watcher"
.Ft int
.Fn notify_watch_begin "struct notify_watcher *watcher"
.Ft int
.Fn notify_watch_cancel "struct notify_watcher *watcher"
.Ft int
.Fn notify_watch_take "struct notify_watcher *watcher" "void *data" "size_t capacity" "size_t *length" "struct notify_watch_cursor *cursor" "uint32_t *flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions retain one latest snapshot for a provider and a cursor for
each observer.
They do not publish to BSDNotify, grant authority, or create threads.
The provider validates its typed values, authorizes subscribers, and wakes
its event loop after publishing a change.
Updates are coalesced; intermediate values are not an event history.
.Pp
.Fn notify_watch_create
allocates a fixed buffer and sets a subscriber limit.
Capacity is between 1 and
.Dv NOTIFY_WATCH_MAX_BYTES ;
the subscriber limit is between 1 and
.Dv NOTIFY_WATCH_MAX_SUBSCRIBERS .
No snapshot exists until the first publish, which may have zero length.
Publishing does not allocate memory.
Identical bytes do not advance the generation, so providers must initialize
padding and encode equivalent values consistently.
.Pp
.Fn notify_watch_open
creates an observer.
A NULL or zero resume cursor starts with the current snapshot.
A cursor from a previous instance causes the next delivered snapshot to carry
.Dv NOTIFY_WATCH_RESET .
A cursor in the current epoch cannot name a future generation.
.Pp
.Fn notify_watch_begin
starts one watch; another begin while pending fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Fn notify_watch_take
returns 1 after copying a changed snapshot and atomically advancing the cursor,
0 when no changed snapshot is available, or -1 on error.
A successful take completes the watch.
When the output buffer is too small,
.Er EMSGSIZE
is returned and
.Fa length
receives the required size; the watch and cursor remain unchanged.
A provider whose subsequent transport delivery fails must close the observer
or reopen it from its last acknowledged cursor.
.Pp
.Fn notify_watch_cancel
ends a pending watch without advancing its cursor.
Closing an observer cancels its watch and releases its subscriber slot.
Destroying a store with live observers fails with
.Er EBUSY .
Generation exhaustion fails with
.Er EOVERFLOW
without replacing the retained value.
.Pp
Store access is protected by a mutex.
Calls using the same observer, including close, must be serialized by the
caller.
Creation and destruction require exclusive ownership of the store.
These objects cannot be used in a child after fork without exec.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Create, destroy, open, begin and cancel return 0 on success and -1 on error.
Publish returns 1 for a changed snapshot, 0 for identical data, and -1 on error.
Take has the return values described above.
Errors set
.Va errno .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libnotify 3
